        "at": "2026-11-19T23:32:57.816Z"
      }
    },
    "c5": {
      "anchor": "p-file-upload-in-spell",
      "kind": "phase",
      "label": "File Upload In Spell",
      "excerpt": "File Upload In Spell",
      "text": "Also, what will this look like?",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-19T23:37:36.000Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-19T23:44:27.524Z",
          "html": "<p>Like this, made from Spell UI's pieces. The drop area is shown at rest, then with files dragged over it, then with a row for each file. P9's plan shows the same pictures.</p>\n<p><img src=\"/epics/from-jarvis/pictures/p9-uploader-light.png\" alt=\"The uploader, light\" width=\"720\" /></p>\n<p><img src=\"/epics/from-jarvis/pictures/p9-uploader-dark.png\" alt=\"The uploader, dark\" width=\"720\" /></p>\n<ul>\n  <li>The Choose Files button is the real <code>&lt;ui-input type=\"file\"&gt;</code>, and the progress bar is <code>&lt;ui-progress&gt;</code>.</li>\n  <li>Each row shows how its file is doing: uploading, uploaded, too big, the wrong kind, or failed with the server's error.</li>\n  <li>The ✕ removes a file, or stops it uploading.</li>\n  <li>With <code>drop-zone=\"page\"</code>, the whole page gets the same blue highlight while files are dragged over it.</li>\n</ul>"
        }
      ],
      "claim": {
        "by": "owenoak",
        "agent": "claude",
        "at": "2026-11-19T23:38:10.739Z"
      }
    },
